<title>Nigeria: the situation</title>
<link>https://map.igred.org/crisis/nigeria/</link>
<guid isPermaLink="false">igred-summary-nigeria-2026-11-25T08:56:13.968Z</guid>
<pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 08:56:13 GMT</pubDate>
<description>&lt;p&gt;Bandits continue to attack civilian communities in Zamfara, killing two clerics, abducting an 11‑month-old baby and other residents, while gunmen target Irigwe villages in southern Kaduna and around Kainji Lake. The Nigerian army has responded with ambushes that killed two bandits and recovered weapons, and police operations in Benue have arrested suspects linked to bandit and robbery networks. A 19‑year-old Christian farmer lost a hand in a separate attack, and a land dispute in Niger state sparked dozens of deaths. The conflict recorded 1,486 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Tori News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMioAFBVV95cUxNbFRzSk1DQWJtMnJWcDZDX0J1aG94NEctclMwQUllUlVCWTAwUjRHS0pIYXhSV3NkTzJaSEVlUkkyVGY1aWwtanRvelFnLXVIN0RzOTlDdXdkOUlWMS1aSUt4a3FtWG5FSlk5NVBuc3ZqS3ROSVFlVnYyaEYwTWl4YXhpbTYzRFY3dUpPelNkWEEwdHBvdEJKRlplSzdxTzJn?oc=5&quot;&gt;PM News Nigeria&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMizAFBVV95cUxPdk13ckVKdDZ3aUhlblh4NmY3d1g1czJrcTdsck5ldWdQeXFmZ1FtZFZNVDBKaUVqT0ZNdVBSNXhDUlNDcmk2bGUxaHhRQ1NRV0tsUUdhZWFTMXFYT1lTczNJbFlwM1hwVnE4NklQSTBkVlBTa00yUmFONFFfZGlOanJoazN5TjU2WFBLX18yZzdpWTdFM1VsVFZEZkNjTWRjYjVOU3VsWHRFNWJLdHlHOE90U2E3NUlkRlhPLUFuaU1GcEhKWkFBOVNUcGo?oc=5&quot;&gt;Peoples Gazette Nigeria&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMingFBVV95cUxPeUtGWThhQThvTDZCUWNvUDJIUDJfemZDb291SXNXc3pjbUpHT1AzTUptZk00YlQ4bnNLNTRSWDJRdlJhMjBMaG9JUmdGVjdJUUs3akl4clBrOHVBbzRPVmVZUm0zcHYxRGlNaUk5eXdNb1RxVERPYWIyNWJVZ1MzdkVtTWpZN1FlcDQ1dGtVck9MaGU0aUV3cnhxUjZEQQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Daily Times Nigeria News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirwFBVV95cUxNb3N0c2hxcjRmbjZWU3dGdUFTeG5KaEcwOE1wV1hxbE9VOGRBVnN2MlRVai1JY0J0Ym1kLVg